* Schaum Basic Circuit Analysis, Exercise 3.65 / Fig. 3-30.
* Find the indicated unknown currents using KCL.
* Fig. 3-30 has branch-current annotations but no component values, so this is
* represented as a constraint-only netlist.
*
* Fig. 3-30(a):
*   Right node: I1 + 5 A enters, 4 A + 3 A leaves.
*   Left node: 3 A enters, I1 + I2 + 7 A leaves.
.constraint (eq (add I1 5) (add 4 3))
.constraint (eq (add I1 I2 7) 3)
*
* Fig. 3-30(b):
*   Itop is the upper horizontal branch current, left to right.
*   Ibottom is the lower horizontal branch current, left to right.
.constraint (eq (add 2 Itop) 4)
.constraint (eq (add Itop I4) 5)
.constraint (eq (add Ibottom 6) I4)
.constraint (eq (add I3 2) Ibottom)
